WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.347 --> 00:00:04.014
(sentimental guitar music)

00:00:21.271 --> 00:00:22.163
- Dear Mom.

00:00:22.163 --> 00:00:23.079
- Dear Mom.

00:00:23.079 --> 00:00:23.912
- Dear Mom.

00:00:23.912 --> 00:00:24.745
- [Group] Thank you.

00:00:24.745 --> 00:00:27.374
- My adopted mom, she handles every situation

00:00:27.374 --> 00:00:29.208
you throw at her with such grace,

00:00:29.208 --> 00:00:32.252
and she comes out of it stronger than ever.

00:00:32.252 --> 00:00:35.688
She has the kindest heart and the most compassionate soul,

00:00:35.688 --> 00:00:38.424
and she's just beautiful on the inside and out,

00:00:38.424 --> 00:00:40.264
and if I could be half the woman

00:00:40.264 --> 00:00:41.419
that she is whenever I grow up,

00:00:41.419 --> 00:00:43.185
I've done something right with my life.

00:00:43.185 --> 00:00:45.754
- We don't share the same skin or the same eyes.

00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:46.997
- We don't share the same smile

00:00:46.997 --> 00:00:48.014
or the same laugh.

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:49.416
- We don't share the same nose

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:51.271
or the same taste in most things.

00:00:51.271 --> 00:00:52.104
- But I am

00:00:52.219 --> 00:00:56.052
- [Group] Absolutely, 100%, unequivocally

00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:58.277
- Who I am because of you.

00:00:58.277 --> 00:01:01.521
- Despite my mom and I not sharing any DNA,

00:01:01.521 --> 00:01:05.021
she passed down to me her love for animals

00:01:05.759 --> 00:01:09.441
and the fact that we're both very allergic to all of them.

00:01:09.441 --> 00:01:11.522
- On the outside we look like strangers

00:01:11.522 --> 00:01:13.280
journeying this life together,

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:14.746
but on the inside--

00:01:14.746 --> 00:01:16.996
- [group] I know you, mom.

00:01:17.479 --> 00:01:20.968
- Every time you looked at me and told me that I was chosen.

00:01:20.968 --> 00:01:22.802
- And every time that I wanted to give up

00:01:22.802 --> 00:01:24.347
and if you still love me.

00:01:24.347 --> 00:01:26.094
- Mom, every time that I felt unwanted

00:01:26.094 --> 00:01:27.342
and you looked me in the eye

00:01:27.342 --> 00:01:31.009
and said "You are mine." the more I am, mom.

00:01:31.125 --> 00:01:33.986
- Our relationship was born from a place of loss

00:01:33.986 --> 00:01:35.992
and that's something we will always grieve.

00:01:35.992 --> 00:01:38.930
- And yet, through all of the uncertainty, all the meltdowns

00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:41.166
or the times that I thought that you would quit.

00:01:41.166 --> 00:01:44.522
- For me, because that's all kids like me have known.

00:01:44.522 --> 00:01:45.803
- [Group] You've seen me through.

00:01:45.803 --> 00:01:47.378
- We found each other later in life

00:01:47.378 --> 00:01:50.326
which means we missed out on a lot of firsts.

00:01:50.326 --> 00:01:52.235
- My mom is pretty amazing.

00:01:52.235 --> 00:01:56.253
She was the field trip coordinator at my elementary school,

00:01:56.253 --> 00:01:57.669
she took me to get my first prom dress

00:01:57.669 --> 00:01:59.944
and she even went to my bachelorette party with me,

00:01:59.944 --> 00:02:01.672
which was pretty rad.

00:02:01.672 --> 00:02:04.755
I will always think of her as my mom.

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:09.237
She is my mom and she will always be my mom.

00:02:09.246 --> 00:02:11.666
- My first missed of hers was her first steps,

00:02:11.666 --> 00:02:13.394
her first dance recitals.

00:02:13.394 --> 00:02:14.727
- But it's okay.

00:02:15.202 --> 00:02:16.946
Inside we get to spend the rest of our lives

00:02:16.946 --> 00:02:18.487
creating new firsts.

00:02:18.487 --> 00:02:21.499
Like, our first thanksgiving together.

00:02:21.499 --> 00:02:23.077
- Or the first time I stayed the night at your house

00:02:23.077 --> 00:02:24.594
and felt the sense of safety.

00:02:24.594 --> 00:02:25.585
- Or our first Christmas,

00:02:25.585 --> 00:02:27.457
when you got me that pink fur blanket

00:02:27.457 --> 00:02:30.457
that I still sleep with to this day.

00:02:46.262 --> 00:02:48.512
^(clapping)

00:02:51.995 --> 00:02:54.662
(cries of joy)

00:02:55.492 --> 00:02:56.358
- [Group] Thank you.

00:02:56.358 --> 00:02:57.624
- Our firsts are different than most

00:02:57.624 --> 00:02:59.317
but it'd be our own special to me.

00:02:59.317 --> 00:03:00.699
- You're saying "yes"

00:03:00.699 --> 00:03:02.840
but underneath has taught me that the

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:05.698
hard you is the least of what makes someone a mother.

00:03:05.698 --> 00:03:06.658
- You've taught me--

00:03:06.658 --> 00:03:08.174
- [Group] That family's about choice.

00:03:08.174 --> 00:03:09.672
- And out of all the people in the world,

00:03:09.672 --> 00:03:12.001
I'm so glad that you chose me.

00:03:12.001 --> 00:03:13.781
- We don't share a single strand of DNA,

00:03:13.781 --> 00:03:15.298
but the presence of that wouldn't change

00:03:15.298 --> 00:03:16.957
anything about what we have.

00:03:16.957 --> 00:03:20.290
- [Group] You are absolutely, 100%,

00:03:20.455 --> 00:03:22.788
unequivocally, still my mom.

00:03:22.862 --> 00:03:23.947
- And even if I try,

00:03:23.947 --> 00:03:27.835
I could not have dreamed of a better mother than you.

00:03:27.835 --> 00:03:31.000
- I love you mommy! Happy Mothers Day!

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:34.583
(sentimental guitar music)

